    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0399" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v26/pg373"/>

                <head>90. Map of the Syrian-Israeli Disengagement Lines<anchor n="1" xml:id="d90-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1974-05-31"
                    >Undated</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[See <ref target="#app1map3">Appendix A, map 3</ref>.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d90-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d90-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Records of Joseph Sisco, Box 32, Briefing Book:
                    Syrian-Israeli Disengagement Documents, Under Secretary Sisco. Secret; No
                    Foreign Dissem. The map accompanying the May 31 Syrian-Israeli Disengagement
                    Agreement contained only lines A, A–1, and B. The additional lines—the dots,
                    dots and dashes, and dashes on the west and east sides of the area of
                    separation—represent the zones of troops and armament limitations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
